      "instance_name": "mapping_1",
      "label": "Media bias narrative mapped onto the woman eating crackers",
      "description": "The top text 'when the media blames all violence on black people' is mapped onto the visual of the woman eating crackers, implying that the media's focus on racialized violence is the 'crackers' being consumed, while the real issue (the 'forgotten' element) is overlooked. The woman's action of eating the cracker symbolizes the media's consumption or fixation on this stereotype.",
