      "@type": "TargetCommunity",
      "instance_name": "audience_id",
      "label": "audience description",
      "description": "The target community is individuals who are aware of or engaged with media narratives regarding racialized violence, particularly those who recognize or critique media bias and anti-Black stereotypes. The meme is designed for an audience familiar with the 'crackers' metaphor as a satirical device to highlight the oversimplification or misdirection in media coverage. This includes people who understand the broader context of racialized violence narratives and the harmful implications of criminal behavior associations with Black people. The audience is likely to be online users who consume satirical or critical commentary on media and social issues, and who may be familiar with the meme format using visual metaphors to critique systemic problems. The meme’s humor and critique rely on the audience’s recognition of the stereotype being satirized and the media bias concept being referenced.",
